> > Can you please confirm this pattern, that when we get any =
vulnerability of jetty and fix from Jetty is available, how soon Kafka =
release a new version with this Jetty?
>=20
> If you are urgently needing to adopt a Jetty release on your own =
schedule, rather than Kafka's schedule, you can always adopt new Jetty =
with your current Kafka version using Maven's <dependencyManagement> =
feature. This works for most projects, not just Kafka.
>=20
> Of course then you should test that the new combination works =
acceptably to your requirements, but it at least gives you an =
independent path forward without needing to pressure Kafka maintainers =
on new releases with dependency updates, until the normal release =
process delivers a fixed Kafka artifact.
